# ==============================================================================
# CINESTREAM ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================

# --- Dynamic DNS & HTTPS ---
DUCKDNS_SUBDOMAIN=mycinestream
DUCKDNS_TOKEN=a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d

# --- Storage & Backup Locations ---
NAS_HOST_PATH=/mnt/1tb/nas
BACKUP_HOST_PATH=/mnt/1tb/backups

# --- Stream & Debrid Providers ---
TORBOX_API_KEY=tb_live_your_torbox_api_key_here
PREMIUMIZE_API_KEY=your_premiumize_api_key_here
EASYNEWS_USERNAME=your_easynews_username
EASYNEWS_PASSWORD=your_easynews_password

# --- Metadata & Localization ---
TMDB_API_KEY=your_tmdb_v3_api_key_here
DEFAULT_COUNTRY=ZA

# --- Permissions & System Overrides ---
PUID=1000
PGID=1000
TZ=Etc/UTC

# --- Internal Web Ports ---
CINESTREAM_PORT=3000
AIOSTREAMS_PORT=3001
RADARR_PORT=7878
SONARR_PORT=8989
PROWLARR_PORT=9696
SABNZBD_PORT=8080

# --- Performance & Multi-Thread Tuning ---
NAS_MAX_CONCURRENT_DOWNLOADS=2
NAS_THREADS_PER_DOWNLOAD=6
PROXY_CONNECTIONS=8
PROXY_CHUNK_SIZE_MB=8
PROXY_READAHEAD_MB=64


# ==============================================================================
# FIELD EXPLANATIONS & DOCUMENTATION
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Dynamic DNS & Free HTTPS (DuckDNS & Caddy)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DUCKDNS_SUBDOMAIN:
#   Enter the subdomain name registered at https://www.duckdns.org.
#   Example: If your domain is "mycinestream.duckdns.org", enter "mycinestream".
#   Caddy automatically requests and renews free Let's Encrypt SSL certificates.
#   Remote access: https://mycinestream.duckdns.org
#
# DUCKDNS_TOKEN:
#   The 36-character UUID token displayed at the top of your duckdns.org dashboard.
#   The duckdns container uses this token to update your public IP every 5 minutes.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Host Storage Mount & Config Backups
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NAS_HOST_PATH:
#   Absolute path on your host/NAS where all media and downloads are saved.
#   Example: /mnt/1tb/nas (or /volume1/media on Synology).
#   Shared across CineStream, Radarr, Sonarr, and SABnzbd at /mnt/nas.
#   Subdirectories (/movies, /tv, /downloads) are auto-created on boot.
#   Enables instant atomic hardlinks without slow cross-filesystem disk copying.
#
# BACKUP_HOST_PATH:
#   Absolute path on your host/NAS where automated server backups are stored.
#   Example: /mnt/1tb/backups (or /volume1/backups).
#   The automated backup engine stores daily snapshots for:
#     - /cinestream  -> SQLite database online backup + app_settings.json
#     - /radarr      -> config.xml snapshot + native Radarr zip backups
#     - /sonarr      -> config.xml snapshot + native Sonarr zip backups
#     - /sabnzbd     -> sabnzbd.ini versioned backups
#     - /aiostreams  -> SQLite data database snapshots
#   Retention is automatically managed (keeps last 14 daily snapshots).

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Stream & Debrid Providers (Enter at least one)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TORBOX_API_KEY:
#   Found under Account Settings -> API at https://torbox.app/settings.
#   Format: tb_live_...
#   Provides cloud-cached debrid streams and direct HTTPS downloading.
#
# PREMIUMIZE_API_KEY:
#   Found under Account -> API Key at https://www.premiumize.me/account.
#   Provides cloud debrid caching and multi-threaded HTTPS direct streaming.
#
# EASYNEWS_USERNAME & EASYNEWS_PASSWORD:
#   Your Easynews login at https://account.easynews.com.
#   Enables instant direct Usenet streaming via CineStream, and auto-provisions
#   SABnzbd with news.easynews.com on SSL port 563 with zero manual wizard setup.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Metadata & Localization
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TMDB_API_KEY:
#   Free v3 API key from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api.
#   Powers poster art, cast, trailers, synopses, and release dates.
#
# DEFAULT_COUNTRY:
#   Two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code (e.g. ZA, US, GB, CA, AU).
#   Used to fetch local parental certification ratings (e.g. PG-13, 16, R).

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Permissions & Ports (Advanced)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUID / PGID:
#   User and Group ID for Linux file permissions. Run `id -u` and `id -g` on host.
#   Default 1000 works for standard primary Linux/NAS users.
#
# TZ:
#   Timezone for container logs and scheduled backups (e.g. Etc/UTC, Africa/Johannesburg, America/New_York).
#
# Ports:
#   Internal host port bindings. Change only if you have port collisions.
#   qBittorrent is excluded from this stack as cloud debrid is used instead.
#
# Multi-Thread Tuning:
#   PROXY_CONNECTIONS: Number of concurrent HTTPS chunks fetched when streaming.
#   PROXY_CHUNK_SIZE_MB: Chunk size in MB for smooth high-bitrate 4K playback.
#   NAS_THREADS_PER_DOWNLOAD: Concurrent threads when downloading to NAS cache.
